Leaderna Biostructures provides services and consultancy in the field of structural biology including unique expertise in the crystallization of nucleic acid-based drugs with proteins. With the significant experience gained from 2015 as IIMCB Structural Biology Center, we are able to support both the biotech and pharmaceutical industry in structure-based drug design (SBDD) projects with the emphasis on early and preclinical stages of drug discovery process.

We offer a flexible approach to the most advanced research which comprises:
1. Preparation of expression constructs and recombinant protein production;
2. X-ray crystallography of protein or protein-ligand complexes including unique expertise in the crystallization of protein-nucleic acid complexes;
3. Single-particle cryo-electron microscopy (cryo-EM) with the goal of determining high-resolution structures of macromolecules with a molecular weight ≥100 kDa;
4. Coupled cryo-EM/X-ray crystallography approach which links and integrates the favorable features of both methods;

EXPERIENCE
Over the years of supporting lead optimization process in drug discovery, we have established a well-grounded position in the field of structure-based drug design (SBDD) projects. In the course of cooperation with leading pharmaceutical companies from Europe (e.g., UbiQ Bio, Selvita, Celon Pharma, OncoArendi Therapeutics, Adamed) and from the United States (Ionis Pharmaceuticals), our services have supported drug discovery efforts for such diseases as cancer, asthma, and depression.
Leaderna solved a crystal structure of OncoArendi’s OATD-01 compound with a target protein. The compound is undergoing clinical trials and in the case of positive results will be the first sarcoidosis drug on the market, with a new mechanism of action (first in class).
Over time of extensive collaboration with Ionis Pharmaceuticals, a world leader in RNA-targeted therapeutics, we expanded our expertise in structure determination of nucleic acid-based drugs with proteins.

EMINENT SPECIALISTS
The success of Leaderna derives from the highest level of expertise in science, advanced skills, and the excellent quality of services that are rendered. With the support of renowned experts with distinguished scientific experience in the field of structural biology, we are able to run challenging projects. We closely collaborate with Polish science centers, among others, the Biological and Chemical Research Centre, University of Warsaw.

MB Biosciences is a life science company specializing in  cell–based Products and Services both in vitro and in vivo;

 We provide Liver-specific and Hepatocytes-based  Products and Services: we provide human, rat and mouse hepatocytes  in suspension; ready-to-use hepatocytes  in multiple plate format;  3D hepatocytes spheroid  and  liver organoid ;  hepatocytes culture medium which maintain primary hepatocytes alive up to 4 weeks in vitro. 
We offer perfusion and  hepatocytes isolation services from  WT Mouse and Rat,  transgenic and various disease mouse models; We also provide various Hepatic assays services; 
We provide genotoxicity and mutagenicity analyses -AMES, Genomic deletion, micronucleus assays with best price and quickest  turn around time; 
We offer Permeability-based products and services (intestinal, airway,  BBB, T84, Caco2, MDR1-MDCK, Calu3); Drug-drug interaction services (CYP and UGP induction and inhibition);
We offer In vivo PK and PD study; In vivo xenografts tumor model services and Biomarker discovery.
 MB Biosciences is committed to providing the highest quality products and services with a shortest turnaround time.

SeromYx Systems provides high throughput assays that characterize antigen-specific antibody effector functions, supported by a machine learning computational biology platform, collectively Systems Serology.  Systems Serology can be used throughout the drug discovery and development process:
 - To establish immune markers of disease, progression, or protection and resolution; 
- To screen large panels of monoclonal antibodies for desired function; 
- To support pre-clinical and IND-enabling measurement of induced response or in vitro mAb effector activity; 
- To measure clinical response, biomarkers of activity or progression or in vivo mAb function; 
- To support filings for marketing approval with surrogate endpoints and support for comparability in CMC filings.  

Each project is customized in terms of assay and antigen selection and computational approach, if any, to meet client needs.

SeromYx is certified as compliant with GCLP, and performs studies in compliance with that standard.

KBI Biopharma is a leading contract development and manufacturing organization for the biopharmaceutical industry. We accelerate and optimize drug development and manufacturing programs for our client partners, which range from small start-up biotechs to global pharmaceutical and biotechnology companies and organizations in bio-defense.  Our expertise in biophysical and biochemical protein characterization makes us highly successful in delivering optimal product stability and bioactivity for our clients. 

Our Core Facilities include:
*Mass Spec Core Facility: KBI’s state-of-the-art mass spectrometry core facility delivers unparalleled structural characterization services to our clients.
*Particle Characterization Core Facility: KBI’s Particle Characterization Core Facility provides specialized, state-of-the-art analysis for subvisible particles ranging in size from nanometer to micron.   

Our core capabilities include: 
*Cell Line Development; 
*Process Development; 
*Analytical Development; 
*Qualification, Validation; 
*Biophysical Characterization; 
*Formulation Development; 
*Mammalian cGMP Manufacturing; 
*Microbial cGMP Manufacturing; 
*GMP Release and Stability. 

Our scientific, quality and regulatory staff possesses the experience - proven through numerous IND and NDA submissions - to meet the challenges that arise at all stages of drug development.  KBI Biopharma's state-of-the-art facilities are located in North Carolina (at the North Carolina Center for Biomanufacturing in Durham and in the Research Triangle Park) and in Boulder, Colorado.

DRL is an international CRO and R&amp;D company with a biobank of more than 30K cases across different diseases. We offer flexible customizable solutions for clinical and preclinical studies to reduce the costs of drug discovery. Our services include but are not limited to:

- Biospecimen procurement (fresh/frozen tissue, FFPE, RNA, DNA, protein, etc.) from a wide range of disease histologies and DNA mutations (including custom requests);
- Phase 0 platform for human testing of therapeutics;
- Tumor organoid pharmacology assays to test lead/candidate therapeutics (these models are better predictors of anti-tumor activity than 2D or xenograft-based models);
- Development of custom 3D assays for in vitro studies or other applications based on client needs (eg, oncology).

